From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 02:58:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP: keep a start_disabled BSS quiet on interface enable

A BSS with start_disabled=1 starts without beacons. The beacons start
only after the flag is cleared and a beacon update is requested.

If the driver disables the interface in that period and enables it
again, hostapd_iface_enable() calls ieee802_11_set_beacon() for every
started BSS. The beacons of a start_disabled BSS then start too early.

Skip the beacon update for such a BSS. reenable_beacon stays set, so
the beacon update that follows later does a full start of the AP in
the driver.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/src/ap/drv_callbacks.c
+++ b/src/ap/drv_callbacks.c
@@ -2542,7 +2542,8 @@ static void hostapd_iface_enable(struct
 		else
 			hostapd_reconfig_encryption(hapd);
 		hapd->reenable_beacon = 1;
-		ieee802_11_set_beacon(hapd);
+		if (!hapd->conf->start_disabled)
+			ieee802_11_set_beacon(hapd);
 #ifdef NEED_AP_MLME
 	} else if (hapd->disabled && hapd->iface->cac_started) {
 		wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "DFS: restarting pending CAC");
